diff --git a/docs/prizes.md b/docs/prizes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..38dbc7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/prizes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Scoring and prizes
+
+## Authoring and persistence
+
+- **Number of winners** is a required positive integer, default **3**, on both
+  new-quiz and Settings forms. Server validation and SQLite constraints enforce
+  the lower bound. The portable JSON format includes `number_of_winners`; old
+  exports without it import with 3. Runtime scores and winners are not exported.
+- Each game snapshots the configured number alongside its title/questions. Editing
+  quiz settings affects subsequent games, not a game already in progress.
+- `GameQuestion.opened_at` is written once by Start/Next, in the game transition's
+  transaction. `Answer.picked_at` is written on **every accepted pick**, including
+  a second tap on the same option. Rejected/late submissions do not change it.
+- Both timestamps are server-owned, stored at microsecond precision. Timing uses
+  server acceptance of the pick, never an untrusted client clock or timestamp.
+  All players share the question's opening time, including late joiners.
+
+## Ranking
+
+`Leaderboard` scores the immutable game snapshots, not editable quiz questions.
+Only the final saved choice on each question counts. A correct choice gives one
+point, regardless of how many options were marked correct. Wrong and unanswered
+questions contribute neither points nor time.
+
+Ordering is descending points, then ascending sum of correct-answer elapsed
+microseconds. An exact score/time tie is resolved by player ID (join order) for
+stable, consecutive places. All joined players rank, even if their presence has
+expired, their name matches someone else's, or they have zero points.
+
+No points or leaderboard are sent to clients while waiting, answering, or viewing
+question feedback. After End quiz, the allowlisted snapshot contains places,
+names, points, and winner flags. The stage renders one `li` per player; phones
+look up their own ID for **Place X of Y**, correctly pluralized points, and the
+optional **You won!** message. No browser keys or private credentials are exposed.
+
+Historical games made before this migration have no reliable opening/pick times.
+They still score their saved answers; missing historical durations contribute
+zero, with stable join-order ties. We do not invent historical timestamps. All
+newly opened questions and accepted picks are timed.
+
+## Awarding prizes
+
+Prize commands use the same authenticated, CSRF-protected endpoint, game lock,
+transaction, and revision check as phase changes. They are valid only after End
+quiz. Replacing winner flags and advancing the revision is atomic.
+
+- **Top N**: first N positive scorers in leaderboard order.
+- **Draw**: everyone strictly above the N-th player's points wins; sample the
+  remaining slots uniformly without replacement from **all** players with the
+  cutoff's points. Speed is ignored for the draw pool.
+- If fewer than N players have points, all positive scorers win. No zero-point
+  player ever wins. Empty games are safe. Each Draw performs a fresh random
+  sample; consecutive draws may legitimately choose the same people.
+- **Reset winners**: clears every winner flag in this game without changing
+  answers, scores, ranks, or another game's winners.
+
+## Live delivery
+
+Phase changes and prize commands publish one authoritative snapshot via Action
+Cable. Production uses Solid Cable in the local SQLite database, polling at
+100 ms; it needs neither Redis nor a worker process. The stage and phones use
+WebSockets, not periodic HTTP as the primary question-delivery mechanism.
+
+**End quiz no longer stops the subscription or reconciliation loop.** Winner
+changes continue to arrive live. Reconnection fetches current persisted state;
+revisions reject stale phase/prize messages. HTTP polling remains a recovery path
+on unreliable Wi-Fi. Phones no longer send presence heartbeats after the quiz,
+but continue state reconciliation and keep their private identity.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `bin/verify`: model/request tests plus local Chromium browser tests.
+- `test/models/prizes_test.rb`: scoring, last picks, precision, tie order, positive
+  counts, cutoff draws, redraws, resets, inactive presence, empty/zero-score games,
+  exact ties, multiple correct options, and independent runs.
+- `test/system/prizes_test.rb`: settings, ordered stage results, phone ranks,
+  singular/zero points, all winner controls, a second stage window, no reloads,
+  and no horizontal phone overflow. HTTP reconciliation is disabled during the
+  live assertions, so they cannot accidentally pass through polling.
+- Production smoke test with `bin/serve` running and moderator credentials set:
+
+  ```sh
+  bundle exec ruby script/prizes_smoke.rb create
+  # Restart bin/serve with the same storage directory and SECRET_KEY_BASE.
+  bundle exec ruby script/prizes_smoke.rb check
+  bundle exec ruby script/prizes_smoke.rb cleanup
+  ```
+
+  This exercises four phones and two stage windows, cutoff ties, zero points,
+  live selection/reset/redraw, post-end reconnection, restart persistence,
+  arbitrary Host acceptance, and local-only browser requests. It measures pushed
+  question delivery with HTTP reconciliation disabled. The verified production
+  run delivered questions in 86–257 ms. Artifacts stay in ignored
+  `storage/verification/`; cleanup removes only its own quiz.
